    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2726" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antandrŏs</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> ), i,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄντανδρος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a maritime town in
				Mysia</i>, now <i>Antandro</i> (acc. to Thuc. 8,
			108, an Æolic colony), <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30,
				32, § 123</span></i>; cf. Mann. Asia Min. 3,
			418.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antandrius</span></b> , a, um, adj., <i>of Antandros</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. ad Q.
				Fr. 1, 2, 2</span></i>.</div>
